import re
p=Path('app/src/replica.css');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
for selector in ['.quick-toggles>button','.quick-toggles>button:hover','.quick-toggles [aria-pressed=true] .preference-switch','.quick-toggles [aria-pressed=true] .preference-switch:before']:
 s=re.sub(re.escape(selector)+r'\{[^}]*\}','',s)
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('app/src/gallery.css');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('.image-viewer[open],.image-viewer[data-open]', '.image-viewer[data-open]');s=re.sub(r'  \.image-viewer::backdrop\{[^}]*\}\n','',s);p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('app/AGENTS.md');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s+='\nHeadless UI Dialog owns Quick Access and the gallery viewer (focus trap, Escape, outside dismissal and scroll lock). Headless UI Switch with Goober styling in ui-styles.js owns theme/Focus toggle states. Do not reintroduce manual modal focus traps or duplicate preference-card CSS. site.config.mjs is the public origin/page metadata/GTM configuration; GTM-PJB889NW is injected only into production HTML. Every known route must ship static Open Graph metadata and the 1200×630 original-photo JPEG. Prioritize the homepage portrait and first project screenshot; keep other galleries lazy/low until interaction.\n';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('DESIGN.md');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s+='\n## Headless UI, social previews, and resource hints — 28 October 2026\nHeadless UI owns modal and switch behavior. Quick Access and the animated image viewer use Dialog/DialogPanel/DialogTitle; Headless UI handles focus containment/restoration, Escape, outside clicks, and scroll locking. MotionConfig supplies gallery transition timing without conflicting with Headless UI’s transition prop. Goober in ui-styles.js owns preference-switch card states and consumes the same canonical CSS variables; retired legacy card rules must not compete with it. The black/navy visual identity, original portrait, and electric TOC arrival remain unchanged.\nOpen Graph uses a 1200×630 original-photo JPEG at /assets/social/rahmawan-og.jpg, composed in og-preview.html. site.config.mjs is the public canonical origin, route metadata and GTM source. Build-time route HTML and explicit Vercel rewrites preserve metadata for crawlers without JavaScript. GTM-PJB889NW is production-only; development emits no Google script/iframe. Fetch Priority gives the portrait/first project image high priority and leaves secondary galleries lazy/low. No additional tracking events or personal contact payloads are added.\n';p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
p=Path('README.md');s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8');s=s.replace('- React 19, JavaScript, and Vite 6.', '- React 19, JavaScript, and Vite 6.\n- Headless UI for accessible dialogs and theme/Focus switches; Goober for shared preference-control styling.')
s=s.replace('- Vercel hosting with an SPA fallback for direct page URLs.', '- Static per-route Open Graph/Twitter metadata, a 1200×630 original-photo social image, and canonical URLs.\n- Fetch Priority hints for critical images and fonts; secondary screenshots stay lazy/low priority.\n- Google Tag Manager container `GTM-PJB889NW`, injected only by production builds.\n- Vercel hosting with explicit metadata-page rewrites and an SPA fallback for other URLs.')
s=s.replace('## Run locally','## Social previews and tracking\n\n![Open Graph preview with Rahmawan’s original photograph](app/public/assets/social/rahmawan-og.jpg)\n\n`app/site.config.mjs` holds the public site URL, per-page titles/descriptions, image path, and GTM container ID. `npm run build` produces raw HTML for all five routes, so link-preview crawlers do not need JavaScript. The actual GTM container is available from Google (HTTP 200 verified during setup). `npm run dev` omits GTM; production builds include the asynchronous loader and noscript fallback. Publishing tags remains controlled in the owner’s GTM workspace.\n\nThe homepage portrait and the first project screenshot receive high fetch priority. Other gallery images stay lazy/low priority until selected; the enlarged image viewer fetches its visible image eagerly.\n\n## Run locally')
s=s.replace('npm run test:sites\n','npm run test:sites\nnpm run test:metadata\n')
s=s.replace('  QuickAccess.jsx      Theme and Focus dialog','  QuickAccess.jsx      Headless UI theme and Focus dialog\n  ui-styles.js         Goober styles for Headless UI switches')
s=s.replace('app/public/assets/\n','app/site.config.mjs    Public metadata, canonical origin, and GTM ID\napp/scripts/\n  page-head.mjs        Social metadata and production GTM HTML\n  generate-pages.mjs   Static HTML entries for link-preview crawlers\napp/public/assets/\n  social/              Original-photo Open Graph JPEG\n')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
